{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Vez5SHyV7CNKRvky6BsTiJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始 framing 完全成立。三层证据 (pairwise / per-type / mechanistic) 在 Few-NERD + MAVEN\n  两个数据集、Qwen3-32B + LLaMA-3.3-70B 两个模型上全部通过显著性门槛。Confusability 独立于\n  type count 预测 F1 退化 (partial r≥0.25, p<0.01)，error taxonomy 干净分离两条 channel，\n  SDGD 在两个数据集上均带来 6-8 F1 点增益，匹配 per-type splitting 质量但仅需 20-25% 的\n  API 开销。Headline: \"BCS independently predicts F1 degradation (partial r=0.32,\n  p=0.002 on Few-NERD; pairwise r=0.19, p<1e-9 on MAVEN), with 10-28x type confusion\n  ratio in extreme batches; SDGD improves F1 by 7.6 points on Few-NERD and 6.0 points\n  on MAVEN over single-pass, matching per-type quality at 22% latency cost.\"\n  三条 claim 各有 ≥2 数据集 + ≥2 模型证据支撑，DocRED 提供第三任务 (RE) 泛化。\n  冲 EMNLP 2026 main。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"MAVEN Cross-Task Confusability Replication\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      MAVEN 事件检测 (168 FrameNet event types) 上的 count curve + pairwise BCS-confusion 分析 +\n      per-type partial correlation。跨任务 (NER→ED) 复现核心发现。SCS 矩阵已预计算 (mean=0.216,\n      pairs_above_0.5=119)。\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Count curve (V2 prompt, Qwen3-32B) ---\n      count_curve_count_1: {f1: 0.33, precision: 0.22, recall: 0.66, pred_gold: 3.0}\n      count_curve_count_5: {f1: 0.29, precision: 0.23, recall: 0.39, pred_gold: 1.70}\n      count_curve_count_15: {f1: 0.24, precision: 0.24, recall: 0.24, pred_gold: 1.00}\n      count_curve_count_30: {f1: 0.19, precision: 0.24, recall: 0.16, pred_gold: 0.67}\n      count_curve_count_60: {f1: 0.13, precision: 0.22, recall: 0.09, pred_gold: 0.41}\n      count_curve_count_120: {f1: 0.08, precision: 0.18, recall: 0.05, pred_gold: 0.28}\n      count_curve_count_168: {f1: 0.06, precision: 0.15, recall: 0.04, pred_gold: 0.27}\n      recall_monotonic_decrease: \"0.66 → 0.04\"\n      wrong_type_trend: \"0 → 11500, monotonic increase\"\n      # --- Pairwise BCS-confusion ---\n      pairwise_pearson_r: 0.19\n      pairwise_pearson_p: 8.4e-10\n      pairwise_n_pairs: 14028\n      pairwise_spearman_rho: 0.23\n      pairwise_spearman_p: 1.6e-11\n      nonzero_spearman_rho: 0.31\n      nonzero_spearman_p: 2.8e-07\n      top_confused_pair: \"Conquering ↔ Attack (SCS=0.837, confusion=89)\"\n      # --- Per-type partial ---\n      per_type_partial_r: 0.22\n      per_type_partial_p: 0.004\n      per_type_n: 168\n      # --- Confusion ratio (extreme batches) ---\n      confusion_ratio_extreme_count_15: 15.2\n      confusion_ratio_extreme_count_30: 12.8\n      # --- 同时附 Few-NERD per-type reanalysis 作为 baseline ---\n      fewnerd_per_type_partial_r: 0.32\n      fewnerd_per_type_partial_p: 0.002\n      fewnerd_per_type_n: 66\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 的 168 种 FrameNet event types 具有已知的层级结构和 sibling confusion\n      (14.6-19.8%)，这是 confusability 效应的天然放大器。Type 空间是 Few-NERD 的 2.5 倍，\n      导致 count curve 退化更剧烈 (recall 从 0.66 跌至 0.04)。Pairwise r=0.19\n      高于 Few-NERD 的 0.156，因为 FrameNet siblings (如 Conquering/Attack,\n      Killing/Death) 在语义空间中高度重叠，而这些 sibling pairs 正是实际推理中\n      最常混淆的。14028 个 type pairs 提供强统计功效，p 值进入 1e-10 量级。\n      Per-type partial r=0.22 (p=0.004) 虽低于 Few-NERD 的 0.32，但仍通过 p<0.01 门槛；\n      这是因为 MAVEN type frequency 分布更偏斜 (长尾更明显)，控制频率后残余方差较大。\n      Confusion ratio 15.2x 表明 extreme high-BCS batches 产生的 type 混淆是 low-BCS\n      的 15 倍，与 Few-NERD 的 10-28x 同一量级。Recall 的单调下降\n      (0.66→0.04) 在更大 type 空间下呈现近似 log-linear 衰减。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 2: MAVEN Count Curve (Qwen3-32B, V2 prompt)\"\n        columns: [\"Count\", \"F1\", \"Precision\", \"Recall\", \"Pred/Gold\", \"WrongType\"]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 0.33, 0.22, 0.66, 3.0, 0]\n          - [5, 0.29, 0.23, 0.39, 1.70, 420]\n          - [15, 0.24, 0.24, 0.24, 1.00, 1850]\n          - [30, 0.19, 0.24, 0.16, 0.67, 3600]\n          - [60, 0.13, 0.22, 0.09, 0.41, 6200]\n          - [120, 0.08, 0.18, 0.05, 0.28, 9100]\n          - [168, 0.06, 0.15, 0.04, 0.27, 11500]\n      - title: \"Table 3: Cross-Dataset Pairwise BCS-Confusion Correlation\"\n        columns: [\"Dataset\", \"Task\", \"n_types\", \"n_pairs\", \"Pearson r\", \"p\", \"Spearman ρ\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Few-NERD\", \"NER\", 66, 1953, 0.156, \"4.6e-12\", 0.160, \"1.3e-12\"]\n          - [\"MAVEN\", \"ED\", 168, 14028, 0.190, \"8.4e-10\", 0.230, \"1.6e-11\"]\n      - title: \"Table 4: Per-Type Partial Correlation r(F1, mean_BCS | log_freq)\"\n        columns: [\"Dataset\", \"n_types\", \"Partial r\", \"p\", \"Verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Few-NERD\", 66, 0.32, 0.002, \"PASS\"]\n          - [\"MAVEN\", 168, 0.22, 0.004, \"PASS\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 2a: MAVEN count curve — recall (blue), precision (orange), F1 (green) vs type count [1..168]。Recall 近似 log-linear 下降，precision 先升后平，F1 低位单调递减。与 Few-NERD (Fig 1a) 同框对比。\"\n      - \"Fig 2b: MAVEN pairwise scatter — SCS vs confusion count (14028 points)，density heatmap。High-SCS 区域集中分布高 confusion 点。标注 top-5 confused pairs。\"\n      - \"Fig 3: Cross-dataset per-type partial r 条形图 — Few-NERD r=0.32 vs MAVEN r=0.22，带 95% CI error bar，两者均通过 p<0.01。\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN 完整复现了 Few-NERD 的三层证据结构：(1) 宏观 count curve 显示 168 types 下 recall 退化\n      至 0.04，远比 Few-NERD (0.30) 严重，验证了 type 空间规模放大 capacity bottleneck；\n      (2) pairwise BCS-confusion r=0.19 (p=8.4e-10) 方向一致且效应更强，符合 FrameNet\n      层级结构下 sibling types 高度语义重叠的先验预期；(3) per-type partial r=0.22 (p=0.004)\n      控制频率后仍显著。跨任务 (NER→ED) 复现 + 跨 type 空间规模 (66→168) 的 consistent\n      方向，排除了 task-specific artifact。Few-NERD per-type reanalysis 给出 r=0.32 (p=0.002)，\n      高于 batch-level partial r=0.303 (p=0.026)，因为 per-type 分析消除了 batch\n      composition noise。两个数据集的 per-type partial r 均在 best-tier 范围内。\n\n  - name: \"DocRED Cross-Task Scaling Stress Test\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      DocRED 关系抽取 (96 relation types) 的 count curve + BCS correlation。\n      第三任务 (RE) 泛化验证，type 空间介于 Few-NERD 和 MAVEN 之间。\n    expected_results:\n      count_curve_count_1: {f1: 0.28, precision: 0.18, recall: 0.62, pred_gold: 3.4}\n      count_curve_count_5: {f1: 0.24, precision: 0.19, recall: 0.33, pred_gold: 1.74}\n      count_curve_count_15: {f1: 0.20, precision: 0.22, recall: 0.18, pred_gold: 0.82}\n      count_curve_count_30: {f1: 0.15, precision: 0.21, recall: 0.12, pred_gold: 0.57}\n      count_curve_count_60: {f1: 0.10, precision: 0.19, recall: 0.07, pred_gold: 0.37}\n      count_curve_count_96: {f1: 0.07, precision: 0.16, recall: 0.05, pred_gold: 0.31}\n      pairwise_pearson_r: 0.14\n      pairwise_pearson_p: 0.0002\n      pairwise_n_pairs: 4560\n      per_type_partial_r: 0.21\n      per_type_partial_p: 0.04\n      per_type_n: 96\n      confusion_ratio_extreme: 7.2\n      top_confused_pair: \"spouse ↔ unmarried_partner (SCS=0.892, confusion=34)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      关系类型比实体/事件类型在语义空间中更结构化 (relation types 由 arg1_type + predicate +\n      arg2_type 三元组定义)，导致整体 confusability 水平低于 NER/ED。但同义关系对\n      (spouse/unmarried_partner, founder/creator, capital/administrative_capital) 仍然\n      高度混淆。Pairwise r=0.14 低于 MAVEN 的 0.19 但在 n=4560 下仍显著 (p=0.0002)。\n      Per-type partial r=0.21 (p=0.04) 略低于 p<0.01 严格门槛但通过 p<0.05，\n      作为第三任务补充证据足够。DocRED 的 document-level RE 任务本身难度更高\n      (需要跨句推理)，baseline 性能更低，但 confusability 效应方向完全一致。\n      Confusion ratio 7.2x 较低，反映关系类型的 confusable pair 密度低于 entity subtypes。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table S1 (Supplementary): DocRED Count Curve\"\n        columns: [\"Count\", \"F1\", \"Precision\", \"Recall\"]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 0.28, 0.18, 0.62]\n          - [15, 0.20, 0.22, 0.18]\n          - [30, 0.15, 0.21, 0.12]\n          - [96, 0.07, 0.16, 0.05]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S1: 三数据集 pairwise r 对比条形图 — Few-NERD (NER, r=0.156), MAVEN (ED, r=0.19), DocRED (RE, r=0.14)，均显著。配 task icons。\"\n    analysis: >\n      DocRED 提供第三 IE 任务 (关系抽取) 的泛化证据。Confusability 效应方向一致但效应量\n      较小，符合关系类型语义分离度高于实体 subtype 的先验。Per-type p=0.04 未达 p<0.01\n      严格门槛，但作为 supplementary evidence 足以支撑 \"task-agnostic\" 的 claim。\n      三任务 (NER + ED + RE) × 两模型的一致方向构成强泛化论证。DocRED 结果放 appendix。\n\n  - name: \"Count × Confusability 2×2 Interaction\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      Few-NERD 上 {low count=6, high count=22} × {low BCS, high BCS} 的 2×2\n      factorial design。检验 count 和 confusability 是 additive 还是 multiplicative interaction。\n    expected_results:\n      # --- F1 ---\n      f1_lowcount_lowbcs: 0.42\n      f1_lowcount_highbcs: 0.36\n      f1_highcount_lowbcs: 0.34\n      f1_highcount_highbcs: 0.28\n      count_main_effect_f1: -0.08\n      bcs_main_effect_f1: -0.06\n      interaction_f1: 0.00\n      interaction_p_f1: 0.82\n      # --- Recall ---\n      recall_lowcount_lowbcs: 0.48\n      recall_lowcount_highbcs: 0.46\n      recall_highcount_lowbcs: 0.28\n      recall_highcount_highbcs: 0.26\n      count_main_effect_recall: -0.20\n      bcs_main_effect_recall: -0.02\n      # --- Type Confusion Rate ---\n      confusion_lowcount_lowbcs: 0.005\n      confusion_lowcount_highbcs: 0.045\n      confusion_highcount_lowbcs: 0.012\n      confusion_highcount_highbcs: 0.058\n      bcs_main_effect_confusion: +0.038\n      count_main_effect_confusion: +0.010\n      # --- ANOVA ---\n      anova_count_f: 18.4\n      anova_count_p: 0.0001\n      anova_bcs_f: 11.2\n      anova_bcs_p: 0.002\n      anova_interaction_f: 0.05\n      anova_interaction_p: 0.82\n    result_rationale: >\n      Additive 交互模式是 multi-channel 模型的直接推论：count 通过 attention dilution 影响\n      recall (Channel 1)，confusability 通过 semantic interference 影响 type assignment\n      (Channel 2)，两者在不同认知/计算路径上操作，不应产生显著交互。具体而言：\n      (1) Recall 主要由 count 驱动 (main effect -0.20)，BCS 对 recall 影响微弱 (-0.02)，\n      因为即使类型不混淆，高 count 仍导致 entity omission；\n      (2) Type confusion rate 主要由 BCS 驱动 (main effect +0.038)，count 的贡献较小\n      (+0.010)，因为即使类型数多，如果语义分离度高则不会产生 type substitution；\n      (3) 交互项 F=0.05 (p=0.82) 不显著，表明两个 main effect 的影响是 strictly additive\n      ——降低 count 不会减少 confusability-driven errors，分离 confusable types\n      不会改善 capacity-driven misses。这是 SDGD 设计理念的实验基础：SDGD 专门\n      targeting Channel 2，与 batch size reduction (Channel 1) 正交且可组合。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 5: 2×2 Factorial Results (Few-NERD, Qwen3-32B)\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Low BCS\", \"High BCS\", \"BCS Main Effect\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Low Count (6)\", \"F1=0.42 / R=0.48 / TCR=0.5%\", \"F1=0.36 / R=0.46 / TCR=4.5%\", \"-0.06 / -0.02 / +3.8%\"]\n          - [\"High Count (22)\", \"F1=0.34 / R=0.28 / TCR=1.2%\", \"F1=0.28 / R=0.26 / TCR=5.8%\", \"-0.06 / -0.02 / +3.8%\"]\n          - [\"Count Main Effect\", \"-0.08 / -0.20 / +0.7%\", \"-0.08 / -0.20 / +1.3%\", \"Interaction ≈ 0\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 4: 2×2 interaction plot — F1 (左) 和 type confusion rate (右) 的 interaction lines。两组平行线 (无交互)，左图 count 斜率大，右图 BCS 斜率大。\"\n      - \"Fig 4c: 三指标分离图 — recall 仅随 count 下降 (两条 BCS 线重合)，type confusion rate 仅随 BCS 上升 (两条 count 线重合)，precision 两者均影响。\"\n    analysis: >\n      2×2 结果干净地验证了 multi-channel degradation model：count 和 confusability\n      通过正交通道独立降低抽取质量，无显著交互 (p=0.82)。Recall 几乎完全由 count\n      解释 (main effect -0.20 vs BCS 的 -0.02)，type confusion 几乎完全由 BCS\n      解释 (main effect +0.038 vs count 的 +0.010)。这为 SDGD 的设计理念提供了\n      因果方向的实验支持：优化 batch 内 confusability 可以独立于 batch size reduction\n      改善抽取质量，两者可叠加。\n\n  - name: \"BCS-Binned Error Taxonomy\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      Few-NERD 上按 BCS 分 bin 的系统性 FP 分类 (type_substitution / boundary_error /\n      false_negative / hallucination)。Mechanistic evidence for multi-channel model。\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Error proportions by BCS bin ---\n      bcs_bin_0_to_0.2:\n        type_substitution: 0.08\n        boundary_error: 0.12\n        false_negative: 0.62\n        hallucination: 0.18\n        n_errors: 245\n      bcs_bin_0.2_to_0.4:\n        type_substitution: 0.15\n        boundary_error: 0.10\n        false_negative: 0.55\n        hallucination: 0.20\n        n_errors: 312\n      bcs_bin_0.4_to_0.6:\n        type_substitution: 0.35\n        boundary_error: 0.08\n        false_negative: 0.38\n        hallucination: 0.19\n        n_errors: 280\n      bcs_bin_0.6_to_0.8:\n        type_substitution: 0.55\n        boundary_error: 0.06\n        false_negative: 0.24\n        hallucination: 0.15\n        n_errors: 198\n      bcs_bin_0.8_to_1.0:\n        type_substitution: 0.68\n        boundary_error: 0.05\n        false_negative: 0.15\n        hallucination: 0.12\n        n_errors: 156\n      # --- Summary ---\n      high_bcs_type_sub_pct: 0.68\n      low_bcs_false_neg_pct: 0.62\n      type_sub_monotonic_with_bcs: true\n      false_neg_monotonic_inverse_bcs: true\n      chi_square_independence: 142.3\n      chi_square_p: 2.1e-24\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 best tier 下，error taxonomy 干净分离是 multi-channel 模型最强的 mechanistic\n      证据。High-BCS batches (0.8-1.0) 中 type_substitution 占 68%：当 batch 内包含语义\n      高度相似的类型 (如 person-other 和 person-politician)，模型正确识别 entity span\n      但在 type assignment 阶段发生 interference，将正确 span 标注为语义邻近的错误类型。\n      Low-BCS batches (0-0.2) 中 false_negative 占 62%：当类型语义分离度高，模型不会\n      混淆类型，但由于 attention 需覆盖多种不同类型的 pattern，部分 entity 被完全遗漏\n      (capacity bottleneck)。Type_substitution 从 8% 到 68% 的单调递增、false_negative\n      从 62% 到 15% 的单调递减，形成完美的 crossover pattern。Hallucination 比例\n      (12-20%) 与 BCS 无关，说明幻觉是模型固有特性而非 schema-driven artifact。\n      Chi-square 独立性检验 p=2.1e-24 确认 error type 分布与 BCS bin 高度相关。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 6: Error Taxonomy by BCS Bin (Few-NERD, n=1191 errors)\"\n        columns: [\"BCS Bin\", \"TypeSub%\", \"BoundErr%\", \"FalseNeg%\", \"Halluc%\", \"n\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"[0, 0.2)\", \"8%\", \"12%\", \"62%\", \"18%\", 245]\n          - [\"[0.2, 0.4)\", \"15%\", \"10%\", \"55%\", \"20%\", 312]\n          - [\"[0.4, 0.6)\", \"35%\", \"8%\", \"38%\", \"19%\", 280]\n          - [\"[0.6, 0.8)\", \"55%\", \"6%\", \"24%\", \"15%\", 198]\n          - [\"[0.8, 1.0]\", \"68%\", \"5%\", \"15%\", \"12%\", 156]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5: Stacked area chart — error type 比例 vs BCS bin。TypeSub (红) 从左下到右上递增，FalseNeg (蓝) 从左上到右下递减，形成 X 形 crossover。Hallucination (灰) 保持水平带。\"\n      - \"Fig 5b: 两个代表性 case 的 error 展示 — left: low-BCS batch 中 entity 被完全遗漏 (FN)；right: high-BCS batch 中 'John Smith' 被标为 person-politician 而非 person-other (TypeSub)。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Error taxonomy 提供了 multi-channel 模型的 mechanistic smoking gun。TypeSub ≥60% 在\n      high-BCS 区间 (实际 68%) 和 FalseNeg ≥50% 在 low-BCS 区间 (实际 62%) 均满足\n      best-tier 门槛。这证明 BCS 不仅在统计上与 F1 相关，而且通过可解释的机制起作用：\n      语义相似类型导致 type confusion (Channel 2)，语义分离类型的 capacity 限制导致 entity\n      omission (Channel 1)。Boundary error 和 hallucination 与 BCS 基本无关，排除了\n      confounding explanations。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-Model Validation (LLaMA-3.3-70B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-012\"\n    description: >\n      用 LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct 在 Few-NERD 上复现 exp-002 protocol：count curve +\n      within-count BCS correlation + pairwise BCS-confusion。排除 single-model artifact。\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Count curve ---\n      count_curve_count_1: {f1: 0.30, precision: 0.20, recall: 0.60, pred_gold: 3.0}\n      count_curve_count_6: {f1: 0.29, precision: 0.22, recall: 0.42, pred_gold: 1.91}\n      count_curve_count_12: {f1: 0.32, precision: 0.32, recall: 0.32, pred_gold: 1.00}\n      count_curve_count_22: {f1: 0.28, precision: 0.32, recall: 0.25, pred_gold: 0.78}\n      count_curve_count_44: {f1: 0.40, precision: 0.46, recall: 0.35, pred_gold: 0.76}\n      count_curve_count_64: {f1: 0.38, precision: 0.55, recall: 0.29, pred_gold: 0.53}\n      recall_monotonic: \"0.60 → 0.29\"\n      # --- Pairwise BCS-confusion ---\n      pairwise_pearson_r: 0.14\n      pairwise_pearson_p: 3.2e-10\n      pairwise_n_pairs: 1953\n      pairwise_spearman_rho: 0.17\n      nonzero_spearman_rho: 0.22\n      nonzero_spearman_p: 4.8e-05\n      nonzero_n: 289\n      # --- Within-count correlation ---\n      within_count_6_f1_bcs_r: 0.20\n      within_count_6_f1_bcs_p: 0.31\n      within_count_12_f1_bcs_r: 0.44\n      within_count_12_f1_bcs_p: 0.021\n      partial_f1_bcs_r: 0.28\n      partial_f1_bcs_p: 0.040\n      # --- Cross-model consistency ---\n      top10_confused_pairs_overlap_with_qwen: 7\n      rank_correlation_confusion_matrices: 0.61\n      direction_consistent: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA-3.3-70B 来自不同模型家族 (Meta vs Alibaba)，使用不同的预训练数据和架构\n      细节 (GQA vs MHA, 不同 tokenizer)。Pairwise r=0.14 略低于 Qwen3-32B 的 0.156，\n      处于 best-tier [0.1, 0.2] 范围内。效应略低的原因：LLaMA 的 70B 参数可能提供\n      更强的 type disambiguation 能力，部分抵消 confusability 效应，但不足以消除。\n      p=3.2e-10 极显著，因为 n=1953 pairs 提供充足统计功效。Top-10 confused pairs\n      有 7 对与 Qwen 重合 (如 person-other↔person-politician)，说明 confusability\n      pattern 是 schema 和 task 的固有属性而非 model-specific artifact。两模型的\n      confusion matrix rank correlation=0.61 表明中等到强的一致性。Count curve 形态\n      相似但绝对水平略低 (70B 模型用 FP8 量化可能有轻微精度损失，但趋势不受影响)。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 7: Multi-Model Pairwise BCS-Confusion Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Family\", \"Params\", \"r\", \"p\", \"ρ(nonzero)\", \"p\", \"Top-10 Overlap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", \"Qwen\", \"32B\", 0.156, \"4.6e-12\", 0.254, \"1.1e-6\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"LLaMA-3.3-70B\", \"LLaMA\", \"70B\", 0.140, \"3.2e-10\", 0.220, \"4.8e-5\", \"7/10\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 6: 双模型 confusion matrix heatmap (top-20 types)。Left: Qwen3-32B, Right: LLaMA-3.3-70B。Hotspot 位置高度重合 (person subtypes, location subtypes)。\"\n      - \"Fig 6b: 两模型 pairwise confusion count 的 scatter plot，r=0.61，showing agreement on which pairs are most confusable。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Multi-model validation 排除了 confusability 效应是 Qwen3-32B specific 的可能性。\n      LLaMA-3.3-70B 的 pairwise r=0.14 (p=3.2e-10) 方向一致且高度显著，效应量在\n      best-tier 范围内。两模型 confusion matrix 的 rank correlation=0.61 说明 type pair\n      level 的混淆 pattern 在模型间 transferable——这意味着 embedding-based SCS 作为\n      confusability proxy 不仅对单个模型有效，而且具有跨模型泛化能力。\n      这也意味着 SDGD 的 batch composition 不需要针对每个模型重新计算。\n\n  - name: \"SDGD-zero on Few-NERD\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      Confusability-minimizing batch composition via embedding SCS + graph coloring on\n      Few-NERD (66 types)。与 single-pass full-schema baseline 对比。\n    expected_results:\n      # --- SDGD parameters ---\n      scs_threshold_tau: 0.50\n      n_edges_in_graph: 142\n      chromatic_number: 10\n      avg_types_per_batch: 6.6\n      max_types_per_batch: 9\n      min_types_per_batch: 4\n      # --- Performance ---\n      single_pass_f1: 0.414\n      single_pass_precision: 0.648\n      single_pass_recall: 0.304\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.490\n      sdgd_zero_precision: 0.520\n      sdgd_zero_recall: 0.462\n      f1_gain_over_single_pass: 7.6\n      recall_gain: 15.8\n      precision_delta: -12.8\n      # --- Latency ---\n      single_pass_api_calls: 1\n      sdgd_zero_api_calls: 10\n      single_pass_wall_clock_s: 48\n      sdgd_zero_wall_clock_s: 385\n      sdgd_zero_wall_clock_parallel_s: 95\n      # --- Error analysis ---\n      single_pass_wrong_type_count: 2434\n      sdgd_zero_wrong_type_count: 680\n      wrong_type_reduction_pct: 72\n      # --- Deduplication ---\n      cross_batch_duplicates: 124\n      dedup_strategy: \"highest confidence span retained\"\n      dedup_impact_on_f1: +0.008\n    result_rationale: >\n      SDGD-zero 的 F1 增益 (+7.6 points) 来自两个叠加效果：(1) batch size 从 64 减至\n      avg 6.6 types，缓解 Channel 1 capacity bottleneck，recall 从 0.304 提升到 0.462\n      (+15.8pp)；(2) confusability-aware grouping 确保每个 batch 内无高 SCS pair，减少\n      Channel 2 type confusion，WrongType errors 从 2434 降至 680 (-72%)。Precision\n      轻微下降 (-12.8pp) 是因为小 batch 下模型倾向于 over-predict（与 exp-003a 中\n      low count 的 over-prediction pattern 一致），但 recall 的大幅提升远超 precision 损失。\n      Graph coloring 产生 k=10 batches 是因为 Few-NERD 的 66 types 中约 142 pair SCS>0.5，\n      形成中等密度的 confusability graph，chromatic number 为 10。10 个 batch 的\n      parallelized wall-clock 约 95s (vs single-pass 48s)，开销可接受。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 8: SDGD-zero vs Single-Pass on Few-NERD\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"Prec\", \"Recall\", \"WrongType\", \"API Calls\", \"Wall Clock (s)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass (66 types)\", 0.414, 0.648, 0.304, 2434, 1, 48]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero (k=10)\", 0.490, 0.520, 0.462, 680, 10, 385]\n          - [\"Δ\", \"+7.6pp\", \"-12.8pp\", \"+15.8pp\", \"-72%\", \"+9\", \"+337\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 7a: SDGD batch composition 可视化 — 10 个 batch 的 type 组成 heatmap，颜色编码 SCS。每个 batch 内 cell 均为冷色 (低 SCS)。\"\n      - \"Fig 7b: F1/Recall/Precision bar chart — single-pass vs SDGD-zero。SDGD 的 recall bar 显著高于 single-pass。\"\n      - \"Fig 7c: WrongType error reduction waterfall — 2434 → 680，按 batch 展示 type confusion 的减少。\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-zero 在 Few-NERD 上实现 +7.6 F1 点增益，核心驱动力是 recall 提升 (+15.8pp)\n      和 WrongType reduction (-72%)。Graph coloring 产生的 k=10 batches 在 batch size\n      和 confusability 之间取得平衡——每个 batch 平均 6.6 types 足够小以避免 capacity\n      bottleneck，且 batch 内无 SCS>0.5 的 confusable pair。这是第一个 principled\n      schema decomposition 结果，直接 operationalize 了 Claim 1-2 的发现。\n\n  - name: \"SDGD-zero on MAVEN\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      SDGD-zero on MAVEN (168 event types)。Cross-task validation of SDGD framework。\n      与 single-pass + random batching 对比。\n    expected_results:\n      scs_threshold_tau: 0.35\n      n_edges_in_graph: 1380\n      chromatic_number: 18\n      avg_types_per_batch: 9.3\n      max_types_per_batch: 14\n      min_types_per_batch: 5\n      # --- Performance ---\n      single_pass_f1: 0.08\n      single_pass_recall: 0.05\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.14\n      sdgd_zero_precision: 0.16\n      sdgd_zero_recall: 0.125\n      f1_gain_over_single_pass: 6.0\n      # --- Random batching (same k=18) ---\n      random_k18_f1: 0.11\n      random_k18_recall: 0.095\n      sdgd_vs_random_delta: 3.0\n      # --- Latency ---\n      sdgd_zero_api_calls: 18\n      sdgd_zero_wall_clock_s: 720\n      # --- WrongType ---\n      single_pass_wrong_type: 11500\n      sdgd_zero_wrong_type: 3200\n      wrong_type_reduction_pct: 72\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 的 168 types 和 FrameNet 层级结构使 confusability 效应更极端。\n      Single-pass F1 仅 0.08 (recall 0.05)，因为 168 types 的 prompt 远超模型的\n      effective schema capacity。SDGD-zero 用 τ=0.35 (比 Few-NERD 的 0.5 低，\n      因为 MAVEN 的 SCS 分布整体偏低 mean=0.216) 构建 confusability graph，\n      graph coloring 得 k=18 batches (avg 9.3 types)。F1 提升 +6.0 points 的来源：\n      (1) batch size 从 168 降到 avg 9.3，recall 从 0.05 提升到 0.125；(2) batch 内\n      无 FrameNet sibling pair，WrongType 从 11500 降到 3200 (-72%)。Random batching\n      (same k=18) 只得到 F1=0.11 (+3pp vs single-pass)，因为随机分组仅获得\n      count reduction 收益但不消除 confusability (random 的 batch 内仍有\n      ~7% 的高 SCS pairs)。SDGD vs random Δ=3.0 points 精确量化了\n      confusability-aware grouping 在 count reduction 之上的额外贡献。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 9: SDGD-zero vs Baselines on MAVEN (168 types)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"Prec\", \"Recall\", \"WrongType\", \"API Calls\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass (168)\", 0.08, 0.15, 0.05, 11500, 1]\n          - [\"Random (k=18)\", 0.11, 0.14, 0.095, 5800, 18]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero (k=18)\", 0.14, 0.16, 0.125, 3200, 18]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 8: MAVEN comparison bar chart — single-pass vs random vs SDGD-zero。三组 F1/Recall/WrongType bars。SDGD 在所有指标上优于 random，random 优于 single-pass。\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-zero 在 MAVEN 上的 +6.0 F1 增益 (和 vs random 的 +3.0 Δ) 证明 confusability-\n      aware decomposition 跨任务有效。MAVEN 的更大 type 空间 (168 vs 66) 使 count\n      reduction 本身就带来显著收益 (random +3pp)，但 SDGD 在此基础上再加 3pp，\n      量化了 confusability channel 的独立贡献。\n\n  - name: \"SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      用 5-10 个 calibration examples 构建 empirical confusion matrix，替代 embedding SCS\n      进行 graph coloring。与 SDGD-zero 对比。\n    expected_results:\n      calibration_examples: 8\n      calibration_api_calls: 8\n      calibration_wall_clock_s: 380\n      empirical_confusion_pairs_detected: 86\n      # --- Performance ---\n      sdgd_cal_f1: 0.505\n      sdgd_cal_precision: 0.530\n      sdgd_cal_recall: 0.483\n      sdgd_cal_k: 9\n      f1_gain_over_sdgd_zero: 1.5\n      f1_gain_over_single_pass: 9.1\n      # --- Comparison ---\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.490\n      sdgd_cal_vs_zero_delta: 1.5\n      # --- SCS vs empirical agreement ---\n      scs_empirical_overlap_top50: 0.72\n    result_rationale: >\n      SDGD-cal 通过 8 个 calibration 样本捕获 model-specific 的 confusion pattern，\n      而非依赖通用 embedding 距离。Empirical confusion matrix 发现了 86 个实际 confusion\n      pairs，其中 72% 也被 SCS 预测到，但有 28% 是 SCS 遗漏的 (如模型对特定 entity\n      naming pattern 的 confusion，不完全由 type label embedding 距离预测)。这些\n      额外信息使 graph coloring 更精确，产生 k=9 batches (vs SDGD-zero 的 k=10)，\n      实际更少 batch 但 confusability 分离更彻底。F1 提升 +1.5pp over SDGD-zero，\n      主要来自 recall (+2.1pp) 和 WrongType 进一步减少。增益幅度有限 (1.5pp) 是因为\n      embedding SCS 已经是 decent proxy (72% overlap)，calibration 只修正了 edge cases。\n      额外的 8 API calls 用于 calibration，total overhead 可接受。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 10: SDGD Variants Comparison (Few-NERD)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"Prec\", \"Recall\", \"k\", \"Total API Calls\", \"Setup Cost\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass\", 0.414, 0.648, 0.304, 1, 1, \"—\"]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero\", 0.490, 0.520, 0.462, 10, 10, \"0 (embedding only)\"]\n          - [\"SDGD-cal\", 0.505, 0.530, 0.483, 9, \"9+8cal=17\", \"8 calibration runs\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 9: SDGD-zero vs SDGD-cal 的 batch composition 对比 — 两组 heatmap 显示 calibration 如何调整 batch 分配 (标注移动的 types)。\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-cal 比 SDGD-zero 提升 1.5 F1 点，验证了 empirical confusability 优于\n      embedding proxy。但提升幅度有限，说明 SCS embedding 已经是 reasonably good proxy，\n      这反过来支持了 SCS 作为 practical zero-shot confusability measure 的可用性。\n      SDGD-cal 的 9.1pp gain over single-pass 接近 best-tier 上限 (10pp)。\n\n  - name: \"SDGD-cal on MAVEN\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: >\n      SDGD-cal on MAVEN (168 types) with calibration。Full comparison table。\n    expected_results:\n      calibration_examples: 10\n      calibration_api_calls: 10\n      sdgd_cal_f1: 0.16\n      sdgd_cal_precision: 0.175\n      sdgd_cal_recall: 0.148\n      sdgd_cal_k: 16\n      f1_gain_over_single_pass: 8.0\n      f1_gain_over_sdgd_zero: 2.0\n      sdgd_cal_vs_random_delta: 5.0\n      sdgd_cal_wrong_type: 2400\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 的 FrameNet 层级使 calibration 的价值更高：embedding SCS 对 hierarchically\n      related 但 functionally distinct 的 event types (如 Becoming_a_member vs Participation)\n      可能过估 confusability，而 calibration 发现这些 pair 实际不常混淆。反之，某些\n      linguistically similar triggers (如 \"killed\" → Killing vs Death) 的 confusion 被\n      SCS 低估但 calibration 捕获。结果 SDGD-cal 比 SDGD-zero 多 2.0pp (vs Few-NERD\n      的 1.5pp)，因为更大 type 空间下 SCS proxy error 的累积效应更明显。k=16 < SDGD-zero\n      的 k=18，fewer batches 但 confusability 分离更优，总 API 开销更低。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 11: Full MAVEN Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"Prec\", \"Recall\", \"WrongType\", \"k\", \"API Calls\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass\", 0.08, 0.15, 0.05, 11500, 1, 1]\n          - [\"Random (k=18)\", 0.11, 0.14, 0.095, 5800, 18, 18]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero\", 0.14, 0.16, 0.125, 3200, 18, 18]\n          - [\"SDGD-cal\", 0.16, 0.175, 0.148, 2400, 16, \"16+10cal=26\"]\n          - [\"Per-type\", 0.145, 0.13, 0.165, 450, 168, 168]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 10: Full comparison radar chart — 5 methods × 4 metrics (F1, Recall, 1-WrongType_rate, 1/API_calls)。SDGD-cal 在 quality-efficiency frontier 上 dominant。\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN full comparison 展示 SDGD-cal 在 quality-efficiency Pareto frontier 上的\n      优势：F1=0.16 略高于 per-type 的 0.145 (ratio=1.10)，API 开销仅 26 vs 168 calls。\n      Per-type recall 更高 (0.165 vs 0.148) 但 precision 更低 (0.13 vs 0.175)，因为\n      per-type 的单类型 batch 导致严重 over-prediction (没有 cross-type context\n      约束)。SDGD-cal 保留了 batch 内 non-confusable types 的 cross-type context，\n      对 precision 有正面效果。\n\n  - name: \"Random Batching Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: >\n      Few-NERD 上 random batching (same k=10 as SDGD)。\n      隔离 confusability-aware grouping vs batch count reduction 的各自贡献。\n    expected_results:\n      random_k10_f1: 0.455\n      random_k10_precision: 0.490\n      random_k10_recall: 0.425\n      random_k10_wrong_type: 1580\n      random_k10_avg_batch_bcs: 0.42\n      sdgd_zero_avg_batch_bcs: 0.18\n      # --- Decomposition ---\n      gain_from_count_reduction: 4.1\n      gain_from_confusability_reduction: 3.5\n      total_sdgd_gain: 7.6\n      additivity_ratio: 1.0\n      # --- Variance across random seeds ---\n      random_f1_std_across_5_seeds: 0.012\n      random_f1_range: [0.441, 0.468]\n      sdgd_consistently_better: true\n      # --- Significance ---\n      paired_t_sdgd_vs_random: 4.82\n      paired_t_p: 0.0004\n    result_rationale: >\n      Random batching with k=10 将 66 types 随机分成 10 组 (avg 6.6 per batch)，\n      获得与 SDGD 相同的 count reduction 但不优化 confusability。F1=0.455 vs\n      single-pass 0.414 = +4.1pp，纯 count reduction 贡献。SDGD F1=0.490 vs\n      random 0.455 = +3.5pp，纯 confusability reduction 贡献。两者近乎 additive\n      (4.1 + 3.5 = 7.6 = total gain)，与 exp-006 的 2×2 additive interaction 一致。\n      Random 的 avg batch BCS=0.42 (未优化，随机分配时 confusable pairs 仍有 ~35%\n      概率同批)，SDGD 的 avg batch BCS=0.18 (graph coloring 确保无 SCS>0.5 pair)。\n      WrongType: random 1580 vs SDGD 680——random 比 single-pass (2434) 减少 35%\n      (仅因 batch size 减小导致部分 confusable pairs 被分开)，SDGD 减少 72%\n      (系统性消除)。5 random seeds 的 F1 std=0.012 表明 random 结果相对稳定，\n      SDGD 在所有 seed 下 consistently better (paired t-test p=0.0004)。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 12: Gain Decomposition (Few-NERD)\"\n        columns: [\"Source\", \"ΔF1\", \"ΔRecall\", \"ΔWrongType\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Count reduction (random−SP)\", \"+4.1pp\", \"+12.1pp\", \"−35%\"]\n          - [\"Confusability reduction (SDGD−random)\", \"+3.5pp\", \"+3.7pp\", \"−57%\"]\n          - [\"Total (SDGD−SP)\", \"+7.6pp\", \"+15.8pp\", \"−72%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 11: Waterfall chart — F1 从 single-pass (0.414) 到 random (0.455) 到 SDGD (0.490)，两段分别标注 count reduction 和 confusability reduction 贡献。\"\n      - \"Fig 11b: 5 random seeds 的 F1 boxplot vs SDGD 的单点 (horizontal line)。SDGD consistently above all random runs。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Ablation 干净地分离了 SDGD 增益的两个来源：count reduction (+4.1pp, 54%) 和\n      confusability reduction (+3.5pp, 46%)。两者近乎完美 additive，进一步验证了\n      multi-channel model。这个结果直接回应潜在 reviewer concern \"为什么不直接\n      random split?\"——因为 random split 丢失了 confusability channel 的全部贡献，\n      在 Few-NERD 上损失 3.5 F1 点。SDGD vs random Δ=3.5pp 在 best-tier [2, 6] 内。\n\n  - name: \"Per-Type Splitting Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: >\n      Per-type splitting (UniNER-style, k=66 batches, 1 type per batch) on Few-NERD。\n      Decomposition 收益上界和 latency-quality tradeoff。\n    expected_results:\n      per_type_k: 66\n      per_type_f1: 0.49\n      per_type_precision: 0.44\n      per_type_recall: 0.55\n      per_type_wrong_type: 0\n      per_type_api_calls: 66\n      per_type_wall_clock_s: 1650\n      per_type_wall_clock_parallel_s: 420\n      # --- Ratios ---\n      sdgd_vs_pertype_f1_ratio: 1.00\n      sdgd_vs_pertype_latency_ratio: 0.23\n      sdgd_vs_pertype_api_ratio: 0.15\n      # --- Per-type drawbacks ---\n      per_type_over_prediction_rate: 2.85\n      per_type_cross_type_false_positives: 890\n      per_type_dedup_conflicts: 312\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-type splitting 完全消除 confusability (每 batch 仅 1 type，WrongType=0)，\n      是 Channel 2 的理论上界。但它有两个代价：(1) 极高 latency (66 API calls，\n      即使 parallelized 也需 420s vs SDGD 的 95s)；(2) 失去 cross-type context——\n      当模型只被告知寻找一种类型时，它倾向于 over-predict (pred/gold ratio 2.85)，\n      将相关但不匹配的 entity 标为目标类型。这导致 precision=0.44 低于 SDGD 的 0.52。\n      F1=0.49 与 SDGD-zero 的 0.490 几乎相同 (ratio=1.00)，因为 per-type 的 recall\n      优势 (0.55 vs 0.462) 被 precision 劣势 (0.44 vs 0.52) 恰好抵消。\n      SDGD 实现了与 per-type 同等的 F1 但仅用 23% 的 wall-clock 时间和 15% 的\n      API calls，这是 SDGD 的核心 value proposition：通过 principled batch\n      composition 在 confusability reduction 和 cross-type context preservation\n      之间取得最优 tradeoff。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 13: SDGD vs Per-Type Splitting (Few-NERD)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"Prec\", \"Recall\", \"WrongType\", \"API Calls\", \"Wall Clock (s)\", \"Parallel (s)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass\", 0.414, 0.648, 0.304, 2434, 1, 48, 48]\n          - [\"Random (k=10)\", 0.455, 0.490, 0.425, 1580, 10, 350, 90]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero (k=10)\", 0.490, 0.520, 0.462, 680, 10, 385, 95]\n          - [\"SDGD-cal (k=9)\", 0.505, 0.530, 0.483, 520, 17, 560, 130]\n          - [\"Per-type (k=66)\", 0.490, 0.440, 0.550, 0, 66, 1650, 420]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 12: Quality-Latency Pareto frontier — x-axis: parallel wall-clock (log scale), y-axis: F1。Five methods 标注。SDGD-zero 和 SDGD-cal 在 frontier 上，per-type 在 frontier 外 (high latency, same/lower F1)。\"\n      - \"Fig 12b: Precision-Recall tradeoff scatter — per-type (high recall, low precision), SDGD (balanced), single-pass (high precision, low recall)。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-type splitting 验证了 confusability elimination 的理论上界 (WrongType=0)，\n      但 SDGD 以 1/4 的计算开销达到同等 F1。关键 insight：per-type splitting\n      over-corrects——消除 confusability 的同时也消除了 beneficial cross-type context\n      (模型知道其他类型存在时会更 conservative/precise about each type)。SDGD 保留\n      non-confusable types 在同一 batch 内的 mutual constraint effect，实现更好的\n      precision-recall balance。F1 ratio=1.00, latency ratio=0.23，均在 best-tier 范围内。\n\n  - name: \"SCS Embedding Proxy Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-015\"\n    description: >\n      Embedding SCS 与 empirical confusion matrix 的 rank correlation。\n      验证 embedding proxy 的实际有效性。\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Few-NERD ---\n      fewnerd_spearman_rho: 0.52\n      fewnerd_spearman_p: 1.8e-15\n      fewnerd_kendall_tau: 0.41\n      fewnerd_kendall_p: 3.2e-12\n      fewnerd_n_pairs: 1953\n      fewnerd_top20_overlap: 0.75\n      # --- MAVEN ---\n      maven_spearman_rho: 0.48\n      maven_spearman_p: 2.4e-18\n      maven_kendall_tau: 0.37\n      maven_kendall_p: 8.1e-15\n      maven_n_pairs: 14028\n      maven_top20_overlap: 0.70\n      # --- Threshold analysis ---\n      optimal_scs_threshold_fewnerd: 0.48\n      optimal_scs_threshold_maven: 0.33\n      threshold_f1_sensitivity: \"±0.1 around optimal → <1pp F1 change\"\n      # --- Failure cases ---\n      false_negative_pairs: 14\n      false_negative_example: \"product-food ↔ product-drink (SCS=0.38, empirical confusion=45)\"\n      false_positive_pairs: 22\n      false_positive_example: \"event-protest ↔ event-election (SCS=0.71, empirical confusion=2)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Embedding SCS 基于 type label 的语义 embedding 距离，与 empirical confusion 的\n      相关性取决于：(1) type confusion 是否主要由 label 语义相似性驱动 (是的，exp-002\n      已证明)，(2) embedding 空间是否准确反映 LLM 的内部 type representation (大体是，\n      因为都基于 transformer language model)。Spearman ρ=0.52 (Few-NERD) / 0.48 (MAVEN)\n      表示中等到强的 rank agreement。非 perfect (ρ<1) 的原因：(a) 某些 confusion 由\n      context 和 surface form 驱动而非 label semantics (如 person-other 和 person-artist\n      的 confusion 因为实际文本中 artist 常出现在 generic person context)；\n      (b) embedding distance 是对称的但 confusion 可能不对称 (A→B confusion ≠ B→A)。\n      Top-20 overlap 75% 说明 embedding proxy 捕获了大部分 critical confusion pairs。\n      14 个 false negative pairs (SCS 低但实际常混淆) 正好是 SDGD-cal 能额外捕获的，\n      解释了 SDGD-cal 比 SDGD-zero 提升 1.5pp 的来源。Threshold sensitivity ±0.1\n      导致 <1pp F1 change 说明 SDGD 对 τ 选择 robust。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table S2 (Supplementary): SCS Proxy Validation\"\n        columns: [\"Dataset\", \"Spearman ρ\", \"p\", \"Kendall τ\", \"p\", \"Top-20 Overlap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Few-NERD\", 0.52, \"1.8e-15\", 0.41, \"3.2e-12\", \"75%\"]\n          - [\"MAVEN\", 0.48, \"2.4e-18\", 0.37, \"8.1e-15\", \"70%\"]\n      - title: \"Table S3: SCS Threshold Sensitivity\"\n        columns: [\"τ\", \"SDGD k (FN)\", \"F1 (FN)\", \"SDGD k (MV)\", \"F1 (MV)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [0.3, 14, 0.484, 22, 0.135]\n          - [0.4, 12, 0.488, 20, 0.138]\n          - [0.5, 10, 0.490, 18, 0.140]\n          - [0.6, 8, 0.485, 15, 0.136]\n          - [0.7, 6, 0.470, 12, 0.125]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S2: SCS vs empirical confusion scatter — 每个点是一个 type pair，x=SCS, y=empirical confusion count。标注 false positive 和 false negative regions。\"\n      - \"Fig S3: Threshold sensitivity curve — x=τ, y=F1。平坦区间 [0.3, 0.6] 表明 SDGD robust to threshold choice。\"\n    analysis: >\n      SCS embedding proxy 在 ρ=0.48-0.52 水平有效，对 SDGD-zero 的实际性能足够。\n      Threshold sensitivity 分析显示 τ 在 [0.3, 0.6] 区间内 F1 变化 <1pp，使\n      SDGD-zero 成为 truly zero-shot method (无需 calibration 即可 deploy)。\n      False negative analysis 为 SDGD-cal 的额外价值提供了解释：calibration 发现\n      了 14 个 SCS 遗漏的 confusion pairs，将它们分到不同 batch 后 F1 额外提升 1.5pp。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14512,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14512},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d59d397-8bee-498e-9e04-81525269ad2b","uuid":"df3c3d1d-eb15-4c67-ae88-2ff4f912b613"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":621177,"duration_api_ms":622544,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始 framing 完全成立。三层证据 (pairwise / per-type / mechanistic) 在 Few-NERD + MAVEN\n  两个数据集、Qwen3-32B + LLaMA-3.3-70B 两个模型上全部通过显著性门槛。Confusability 独立于\n  type count 预测 F1 退化 (partial r≥0.25, p<0.01)，error taxonomy 干净分离两条 channel，\n  SDGD 在两个数据集上均带来 6-8 F1 点增益，匹配 per-type splitting 质量但仅需 20-25% 的\n  API 开销。Headline: \"BCS independently predicts F1 degradation (partial r=0.32,\n  p=0.002 on Few-NERD; pairwise r=0.19, p<1e-9 on MAVEN), with 10-28x type confusion\n  ratio in extreme batches; SDGD improves F1 by 7.6 points on Few-NERD and 6.0 points\n  on MAVEN over single-pass, matching per-type quality at 22% latency cost.\"\n  三条 claim 各有 ≥2 数据集 + ≥2 模型证据支撑，DocRED 提供第三任务 (RE) 泛化。\n  冲 EMNLP 2026 main。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"MAVEN Cross-Task Confusability Replication\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      MAVEN 事件检测 (168 FrameNet event types) 上的 count curve + pairwise BCS-confusion 分析 +\n      per-type partial correlation。跨任务 (NER→ED) 复现核心发现。SCS 矩阵已预计算 (mean=0.216,\n      pairs_above_0.5=119)。\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Count curve (V2 prompt, Qwen3-32B) ---\n      count_curve_count_1: {f1: 0.33, precision: 0.22, recall: 0.66, pred_gold: 3.0}\n      count_curve_count_5: {f1: 0.29, precision: 0.23, recall: 0.39, pred_gold: 1.70}\n      count_curve_count_15: {f1: 0.24, precision: 0.24, recall: 0.24, pred_gold: 1.00}\n      count_curve_count_30: {f1: 0.19, precision: 0.24, recall: 0.16, pred_gold: 0.67}\n      count_curve_count_60: {f1: 0.13, precision: 0.22, recall: 0.09, pred_gold: 0.41}\n      count_curve_count_120: {f1: 0.08, precision: 0.18, recall: 0.05, pred_gold: 0.28}\n      count_curve_count_168: {f1: 0.06, precision: 0.15, recall: 0.04, pred_gold: 0.27}\n      recall_monotonic_decrease: \"0.66 → 0.04\"\n      wrong_type_trend: \"0 → 11500, monotonic increase\"\n      # --- Pairwise BCS-confusion ---\n      pairwise_pearson_r: 0.19\n      pairwise_pearson_p: 8.4e-10\n      pairwise_n_pairs: 14028\n      pairwise_spearman_rho: 0.23\n      pairwise_spearman_p: 1.6e-11\n      nonzero_spearman_rho: 0.31\n      nonzero_spearman_p: 2.8e-07\n      top_confused_pair: \"Conquering ↔ Attack (SCS=0.837, confusion=89)\"\n      # --- Per-type partial ---\n      per_type_partial_r: 0.22\n      per_type_partial_p: 0.004\n      per_type_n: 168\n      # --- Confusion ratio (extreme batches) ---\n      confusion_ratio_extreme_count_15: 15.2\n      confusion_ratio_extreme_count_30: 12.8\n      # --- 同时附 Few-NERD per-type reanalysis 作为 baseline ---\n      fewnerd_per_type_partial_r: 0.32\n      fewnerd_per_type_partial_p: 0.002\n      fewnerd_per_type_n: 66\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 的 168 种 FrameNet event types 具有已知的层级结构和 sibling confusion\n      (14.6-19.8%)，这是 confusability 效应的天然放大器。Type 空间是 Few-NERD 的 2.5 倍，\n      导致 count curve 退化更剧烈 (recall 从 0.66 跌至 0.04)。Pairwise r=0.19\n      高于 Few-NERD 的 0.156，因为 FrameNet siblings (如 Conquering/Attack,\n      Killing/Death) 在语义空间中高度重叠，而这些 sibling pairs 正是实际推理中\n      最常混淆的。14028 个 type pairs 提供强统计功效，p 值进入 1e-10 量级。\n      Per-type partial r=0.22 (p=0.004) 虽低于 Few-NERD 的 0.32，但仍通过 p<0.01 门槛；\n      这是因为 MAVEN type frequency 分布更偏斜 (长尾更明显)，控制频率后残余方差较大。\n      Confusion ratio 15.2x 表明 extreme high-BCS batches 产生的 type 混淆是 low-BCS\n      的 15 倍，与 Few-NERD 的 10-28x 同一量级。Recall 的单调下降\n      (0.66→0.04) 在更大 type 空间下呈现近似 log-linear 衰减。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 2: MAVEN Count Curve (Qwen3-32B, V2 prompt)\"\n        columns: [\"Count\", \"F1\", \"Precision\", \"Recall\", \"Pred/Gold\", \"WrongType\"]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 0.33, 0.22, 0.66, 3.0, 0]\n          - [5, 0.29, 0.23, 0.39, 1.70, 420]\n          - [15, 0.24, 0.24, 0.24, 1.00, 1850]\n          - [30, 0.19, 0.24, 0.16, 0.67, 3600]\n          - [60, 0.13, 0.22, 0.09, 0.41, 6200]\n          - [120, 0.08, 0.18, 0.05, 0.28, 9100]\n          - [168, 0.06, 0.15, 0.04, 0.27, 11500]\n      - title: \"Table 3: Cross-Dataset Pairwise BCS-Confusion Correlation\"\n        columns: [\"Dataset\", \"Task\", \"n_types\", \"n_pairs\", \"Pearson r\", \"p\", \"Spearman ρ\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Few-NERD\", \"NER\", 66, 1953, 0.156, \"4.6e-12\", 0.160, \"1.3e-12\"]\n          - [\"MAVEN\", \"ED\", 168, 14028, 0.190, \"8.4e-10\", 0.230, \"1.6e-11\"]\n      - title: \"Table 4: Per-Type Partial Correlation r(F1, mean_BCS | log_freq)\"\n        columns: [\"Dataset\", \"n_types\", \"Partial r\", \"p\", \"Verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Few-NERD\", 66, 0.32, 0.002, \"PASS\"]\n          - [\"MAVEN\", 168, 0.22, 0.004, \"PASS\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 2a: MAVEN count curve — recall (blue), precision (orange), F1 (green) vs type count [1..168]。Recall 近似 log-linear 下降，precision 先升后平，F1 低位单调递减。与 Few-NERD (Fig 1a) 同框对比。\"\n      - \"Fig 2b: MAVEN pairwise scatter — SCS vs confusion count (14028 points)，density heatmap。High-SCS 区域集中分布高 confusion 点。标注 top-5 confused pairs。\"\n      - \"Fig 3: Cross-dataset per-type partial r 条形图 — Few-NERD r=0.32 vs MAVEN r=0.22，带 95% CI error bar，两者均通过 p<0.01。\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN 完整复现了 Few-NERD 的三层证据结构：(1) 宏观 count curve 显示 168 types 下 recall 退化\n      至 0.04，远比 Few-NERD (0.30) 严重，验证了 type 空间规模放大 capacity bottleneck；\n      (2) pairwise BCS-confusion r=0.19 (p=8.4e-10) 方向一致且效应更强，符合 FrameNet\n      层级结构下 sibling types 高度语义重叠的先验预期；(3) per-type partial r=0.22 (p=0.004)\n      控制频率后仍显著。跨任务 (NER→ED) 复现 + 跨 type 空间规模 (66→168) 的 consistent\n      方向，排除了 task-specific artifact。Few-NERD per-type reanalysis 给出 r=0.32 (p=0.002)，\n      高于 batch-level partial r=0.303 (p=0.026)，因为 per-type 分析消除了 batch\n      composition noise。两个数据集的 per-type partial r 均在 best-tier 范围内。\n\n  - name: \"DocRED Cross-Task Scaling Stress Test\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      DocRED 关系抽取 (96 relation types) 的 count curve + BCS correlation。\n      第三任务 (RE) 泛化验证，type 空间介于 Few-NERD 和 MAVEN 之间。\n    expected_results:\n      count_curve_count_1: {f1: 0.28, precision: 0.18, recall: 0.62, pred_gold: 3.4}\n      count_curve_count_5: {f1: 0.24, precision: 0.19, recall: 0.33, pred_gold: 1.74}\n      count_curve_count_15: {f1: 0.20, precision: 0.22, recall: 0.18, pred_gold: 0.82}\n      count_curve_count_30: {f1: 0.15, precision: 0.21, recall: 0.12, pred_gold: 0.57}\n      count_curve_count_60: {f1: 0.10, precision: 0.19, recall: 0.07, pred_gold: 0.37}\n      count_curve_count_96: {f1: 0.07, precision: 0.16, recall: 0.05, pred_gold: 0.31}\n      pairwise_pearson_r: 0.14\n      pairwise_pearson_p: 0.0002\n      pairwise_n_pairs: 4560\n      per_type_partial_r: 0.21\n      per_type_partial_p: 0.04\n      per_type_n: 96\n      confusion_ratio_extreme: 7.2\n      top_confused_pair: \"spouse ↔ unmarried_partner (SCS=0.892, confusion=34)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      关系类型比实体/事件类型在语义空间中更结构化 (relation types 由 arg1_type + predicate +\n      arg2_type 三元组定义)，导致整体 confusability 水平低于 NER/ED。但同义关系对\n      (spouse/unmarried_partner, founder/creator, capital/administrative_capital) 仍然\n      高度混淆。Pairwise r=0.14 低于 MAVEN 的 0.19 但在 n=4560 下仍显著 (p=0.0002)。\n      Per-type partial r=0.21 (p=0.04) 略低于 p<0.01 严格门槛但通过 p<0.05，\n      作为第三任务补充证据足够。DocRED 的 document-level RE 任务本身难度更高\n      (需要跨句推理)，baseline 性能更低，但 confusability 效应方向完全一致。\n      Confusion ratio 7.2x 较低，反映关系类型的 confusable pair 密度低于 entity subtypes。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table S1 (Supplementary): DocRED Count Curve\"\n        columns: [\"Count\", \"F1\", \"Precision\", \"Recall\"]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 0.28, 0.18, 0.62]\n          - [15, 0.20, 0.22, 0.18]\n          - [30, 0.15, 0.21, 0.12]\n          - [96, 0.07, 0.16, 0.05]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S1: 三数据集 pairwise r 对比条形图 — Few-NERD (NER, r=0.156), MAVEN (ED, r=0.19), DocRED (RE, r=0.14)，均显著。配 task icons。\"\n    analysis: >\n      DocRED 提供第三 IE 任务 (关系抽取) 的泛化证据。Confusability 效应方向一致但效应量\n      较小，符合关系类型语义分离度高于实体 subtype 的先验。Per-type p=0.04 未达 p<0.01\n      严格门槛，但作为 supplementary evidence 足以支撑 \"task-agnostic\" 的 claim。\n      三任务 (NER + ED + RE) × 两模型的一致方向构成强泛化论证。DocRED 结果放 appendix。\n\n  - name: \"Count × Confusability 2×2 Interaction\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      Few-NERD 上 {low count=6, high count=22} × {low BCS, high BCS} 的 2×2\n      factorial design。检验 count 和 confusability 是 additive 还是 multiplicative interaction。\n    expected_results:\n      # --- F1 ---\n      f1_lowcount_lowbcs: 0.42\n      f1_lowcount_highbcs: 0.36\n      f1_highcount_lowbcs: 0.34\n      f1_highcount_highbcs: 0.28\n      count_main_effect_f1: -0.08\n      bcs_main_effect_f1: -0.06\n      interaction_f1: 0.00\n      interaction_p_f1: 0.82\n      # --- Recall ---\n      recall_lowcount_lowbcs: 0.48\n      recall_lowcount_highbcs: 0.46\n      recall_highcount_lowbcs: 0.28\n      recall_highcount_highbcs: 0.26\n      count_main_effect_recall: -0.20\n      bcs_main_effect_recall: -0.02\n      # --- Type Confusion Rate ---\n      confusion_lowcount_lowbcs: 0.005\n      confusion_lowcount_highbcs: 0.045\n      confusion_highcount_lowbcs: 0.012\n      confusion_highcount_highbcs: 0.058\n      bcs_main_effect_confusion: +0.038\n      count_main_effect_confusion: +0.010\n      # --- ANOVA ---\n      anova_count_f: 18.4\n      anova_count_p: 0.0001\n      anova_bcs_f: 11.2\n      anova_bcs_p: 0.002\n      anova_interaction_f: 0.05\n      anova_interaction_p: 0.82\n    result_rationale: >\n      Additive 交互模式是 multi-channel 模型的直接推论：count 通过 attention dilution 影响\n      recall (Channel 1)，confusability 通过 semantic interference 影响 type assignment\n      (Channel 2)，两者在不同认知/计算路径上操作，不应产生显著交互。具体而言：\n      (1) Recall 主要由 count 驱动 (main effect -0.20)，BCS 对 recall 影响微弱 (-0.02)，\n      因为即使类型不混淆，高 count 仍导致 entity omission；\n      (2) Type confusion rate 主要由 BCS 驱动 (main effect +0.038)，count 的贡献较小\n      (+0.010)，因为即使类型数多，如果语义分离度高则不会产生 type substitution；\n      (3) 交互项 F=0.05 (p=0.82) 不显著，表明两个 main effect 的影响是 strictly additive\n      ——降低 count 不会减少 confusability-driven errors，分离 confusable types\n      不会改善 capacity-driven misses。这是 SDGD 设计理念的实验基础：SDGD 专门\n      targeting Channel 2，与 batch size reduction (Channel 1) 正交且可组合。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 5: 2×2 Factorial Results (Few-NERD, Qwen3-32B)\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Low BCS\", \"High BCS\", \"BCS Main Effect\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Low Count (6)\", \"F1=0.42 / R=0.48 / TCR=0.5%\", \"F1=0.36 / R=0.46 / TCR=4.5%\", \"-0.06 / -0.02 / +3.8%\"]\n          - [\"High Count (22)\", \"F1=0.34 / R=0.28 / TCR=1.2%\", \"F1=0.28 / R=0.26 / TCR=5.8%\", \"-0.06 / -0.02 / +3.8%\"]\n          - [\"Count Main Effect\", \"-0.08 / -0.20 / +0.7%\", \"-0.08 / -0.20 / +1.3%\", \"Interaction ≈ 0\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 4: 2×2 interaction plot — F1 (左) 和 type confusion rate (右) 的 interaction lines。两组平行线 (无交互)，左图 count 斜率大，右图 BCS 斜率大。\"\n      - \"Fig 4c: 三指标分离图 — recall 仅随 count 下降 (两条 BCS 线重合)，type confusion rate 仅随 BCS 上升 (两条 count 线重合)，precision 两者均影响。\"\n    analysis: >\n      2×2 结果干净地验证了 multi-channel degradation model：count 和 confusability\n      通过正交通道独立降低抽取质量，无显著交互 (p=0.82)。Recall 几乎完全由 count\n      解释 (main effect -0.20 vs BCS 的 -0.02)，type confusion 几乎完全由 BCS\n      解释 (main effect +0.038 vs count 的 +0.010)。这为 SDGD 的设计理念提供了\n      因果方向的实验支持：优化 batch 内 confusability 可以独立于 batch size reduction\n      改善抽取质量，两者可叠加。\n\n  - name: \"BCS-Binned Error Taxonomy\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      Few-NERD 上按 BCS 分 bin 的系统性 FP 分类 (type_substitution / boundary_error /\n      false_negative / hallucination)。Mechanistic evidence for multi-channel model。\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Error proportions by BCS bin ---\n      bcs_bin_0_to_0.2:\n        type_substitution: 0.08\n        boundary_error: 0.12\n        false_negative: 0.62\n        hallucination: 0.18\n        n_errors: 245\n      bcs_bin_0.2_to_0.4:\n        type_substitution: 0.15\n        boundary_error: 0.10\n        false_negative: 0.55\n        hallucination: 0.20\n        n_errors: 312\n      bcs_bin_0.4_to_0.6:\n        type_substitution: 0.35\n        boundary_error: 0.08\n        false_negative: 0.38\n        hallucination: 0.19\n        n_errors: 280\n      bcs_bin_0.6_to_0.8:\n        type_substitution: 0.55\n        boundary_error: 0.06\n        false_negative: 0.24\n        hallucination: 0.15\n        n_errors: 198\n      bcs_bin_0.8_to_1.0:\n        type_substitution: 0.68\n        boundary_error: 0.05\n        false_negative: 0.15\n        hallucination: 0.12\n        n_errors: 156\n      # --- Summary ---\n      high_bcs_type_sub_pct: 0.68\n      low_bcs_false_neg_pct: 0.62\n      type_sub_monotonic_with_bcs: true\n      false_neg_monotonic_inverse_bcs: true\n      chi_square_independence: 142.3\n      chi_square_p: 2.1e-24\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 best tier 下，error taxonomy 干净分离是 multi-channel 模型最强的 mechanistic\n      证据。High-BCS batches (0.8-1.0) 中 type_substitution 占 68%：当 batch 内包含语义\n      高度相似的类型 (如 person-other 和 person-politician)，模型正确识别 entity span\n      但在 type assignment 阶段发生 interference，将正确 span 标注为语义邻近的错误类型。\n      Low-BCS batches (0-0.2) 中 false_negative 占 62%：当类型语义分离度高，模型不会\n      混淆类型，但由于 attention 需覆盖多种不同类型的 pattern，部分 entity 被完全遗漏\n      (capacity bottleneck)。Type_substitution 从 8% 到 68% 的单调递增、false_negative\n      从 62% 到 15% 的单调递减，形成完美的 crossover pattern。Hallucination 比例\n      (12-20%) 与 BCS 无关，说明幻觉是模型固有特性而非 schema-driven artifact。\n      Chi-square 独立性检验 p=2.1e-24 确认 error type 分布与 BCS bin 高度相关。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 6: Error Taxonomy by BCS Bin (Few-NERD, n=1191 errors)\"\n        columns: [\"BCS Bin\", \"TypeSub%\", \"BoundErr%\", \"FalseNeg%\", \"Halluc%\", \"n\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"[0, 0.2)\", \"8%\", \"12%\", \"62%\", \"18%\", 245]\n          - [\"[0.2, 0.4)\", \"15%\", \"10%\", \"55%\", \"20%\", 312]\n          - [\"[0.4, 0.6)\", \"35%\", \"8%\", \"38%\", \"19%\", 280]\n          - [\"[0.6, 0.8)\", \"55%\", \"6%\", \"24%\", \"15%\", 198]\n          - [\"[0.8, 1.0]\", \"68%\", \"5%\", \"15%\", \"12%\", 156]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5: Stacked area chart — error type 比例 vs BCS bin。TypeSub (红) 从左下到右上递增，FalseNeg (蓝) 从左上到右下递减，形成 X 形 crossover。Hallucination (灰) 保持水平带。\"\n      - \"Fig 5b: 两个代表性 case 的 error 展示 — left: low-BCS batch 中 entity 被完全遗漏 (FN)；right: high-BCS batch 中 'John Smith' 被标为 person-politician 而非 person-other (TypeSub)。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Error taxonomy 提供了 multi-channel 模型的 mechanistic smoking gun。TypeSub ≥60% 在\n      high-BCS 区间 (实际 68%) 和 FalseNeg ≥50% 在 low-BCS 区间 (实际 62%) 均满足\n      best-tier 门槛。这证明 BCS 不仅在统计上与 F1 相关，而且通过可解释的机制起作用：\n      语义相似类型导致 type confusion (Channel 2)，语义分离类型的 capacity 限制导致 entity\n      omission (Channel 1)。Boundary error 和 hallucination 与 BCS 基本无关，排除了\n      confounding explanations。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-Model Validation (LLaMA-3.3-70B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-012\"\n    description: >\n      用 LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct 在 Few-NERD 上复现 exp-002 protocol：count curve +\n      within-count BCS correlation + pairwise BCS-confusion。排除 single-model artifact。\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Count curve ---\n      count_curve_count_1: {f1: 0.30, precision: 0.20, recall: 0.60, pred_gold: 3.0}\n      count_curve_count_6: {f1: 0.29, precision: 0.22, recall: 0.42, pred_gold: 1.91}\n      count_curve_count_12: {f1: 0.32, precision: 0.32, recall: 0.32, pred_gold: 1.00}\n      count_curve_count_22: {f1: 0.28, precision: 0.32, recall: 0.25, pred_gold: 0.78}\n      count_curve_count_44: {f1: 0.40, precision: 0.46, recall: 0.35, pred_gold: 0.76}\n      count_curve_count_64: {f1: 0.38, precision: 0.55, recall: 0.29, pred_gold: 0.53}\n      recall_monotonic: \"0.60 → 0.29\"\n      # --- Pairwise BCS-confusion ---\n      pairwise_pearson_r: 0.14\n      pairwise_pearson_p: 3.2e-10\n      pairwise_n_pairs: 1953\n      pairwise_spearman_rho: 0.17\n      nonzero_spearman_rho: 0.22\n      nonzero_spearman_p: 4.8e-05\n      nonzero_n: 289\n      # --- Within-count correlation ---\n      within_count_6_f1_bcs_r: 0.20\n      within_count_6_f1_bcs_p: 0.31\n      within_count_12_f1_bcs_r: 0.44\n      within_count_12_f1_bcs_p: 0.021\n      partial_f1_bcs_r: 0.28\n      partial_f1_bcs_p: 0.040\n      # --- Cross-model consistency ---\n      top10_confused_pairs_overlap_with_qwen: 7\n      rank_correlation_confusion_matrices: 0.61\n      direction_consistent: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA-3.3-70B 来自不同模型家族 (Meta vs Alibaba)，使用不同的预训练数据和架构\n      细节 (GQA vs MHA, 不同 tokenizer)。Pairwise r=0.14 略低于 Qwen3-32B 的 0.156，\n      处于 best-tier [0.1, 0.2] 范围内。效应略低的原因：LLaMA 的 70B 参数可能提供\n      更强的 type disambiguation 能力，部分抵消 confusability 效应，但不足以消除。\n      p=3.2e-10 极显著，因为 n=1953 pairs 提供充足统计功效。Top-10 confused pairs\n      有 7 对与 Qwen 重合 (如 person-other↔person-politician)，说明 confusability\n      pattern 是 schema 和 task 的固有属性而非 model-specific artifact。两模型的\n      confusion matrix rank correlation=0.61 表明中等到强的一致性。Count curve 形态\n      相似但绝对水平略低 (70B 模型用 FP8 量化可能有轻微精度损失，但趋势不受影响)。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 7: Multi-Model Pairwise BCS-Confusion Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Family\", \"Params\", \"r\", \"p\", \"ρ(nonzero)\", \"p\", \"Top-10 Overlap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", \"Qwen\", \"32B\", 0.156, \"4.6e-12\", 0.254, \"1.1e-6\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"LLaMA-3.3-70B\", \"LLaMA\", \"70B\", 0.140, \"3.2e-10\", 0.220, \"4.8e-5\", \"7/10\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 6: 双模型 confusion matrix heatmap (top-20 types)。Left: Qwen3-32B, Right: LLaMA-3.3-70B。Hotspot 位置高度重合 (person subtypes, location subtypes)。\"\n      - \"Fig 6b: 两模型 pairwise confusion count 的 scatter plot，r=0.61，showing agreement on which pairs are most confusable。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Multi-model validation 排除了 confusability 效应是 Qwen3-32B specific 的可能性。\n      LLaMA-3.3-70B 的 pairwise r=0.14 (p=3.2e-10) 方向一致且高度显著，效应量在\n      best-tier 范围内。两模型 confusion matrix 的 rank correlation=0.61 说明 type pair\n      level 的混淆 pattern 在模型间 transferable——这意味着 embedding-based SCS 作为\n      confusability proxy 不仅对单个模型有效，而且具有跨模型泛化能力。\n      这也意味着 SDGD 的 batch composition 不需要针对每个模型重新计算。\n\n  - name: \"SDGD-zero on Few-NERD\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      Confusability-minimizing batch composition via embedding SCS + graph coloring on\n      Few-NERD (66 types)。与 single-pass full-schema baseline 对比。\n    expected_results:\n      # --- SDGD parameters ---\n      scs_threshold_tau: 0.50\n      n_edges_in_graph: 142\n      chromatic_number: 10\n      avg_types_per_batch: 6.6\n      max_types_per_batch: 9\n      min_types_per_batch: 4\n      # --- Performance ---\n      single_pass_f1: 0.414\n      single_pass_precision: 0.648\n      single_pass_recall: 0.304\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.490\n      sdgd_zero_precision: 0.520\n      sdgd_zero_recall: 0.462\n      f1_gain_over_single_pass: 7.6\n      recall_gain: 15.8\n      precision_delta: -12.8\n      # --- Latency ---\n      single_pass_api_calls: 1\n      sdgd_zero_api_calls: 10\n      single_pass_wall_clock_s: 48\n      sdgd_zero_wall_clock_s: 385\n      sdgd_zero_wall_clock_parallel_s: 95\n      # --- Error analysis ---\n      single_pass_wrong_type_count: 2434\n      sdgd_zero_wrong_type_count: 680\n      wrong_type_reduction_pct: 72\n      # --- Deduplication ---\n      cross_batch_duplicates: 124\n      dedup_strategy: \"highest confidence span retained\"\n      dedup_impact_on_f1: +0.008\n    result_rationale: >\n      SDGD-zero 的 F1 增益 (+7.6 points) 来自两个叠加效果：(1) batch size 从 64 减至\n      avg 6.6 types，缓解 Channel 1 capacity bottleneck，recall 从 0.304 提升到 0.462\n      (+15.8pp)；(2) confusability-aware grouping 确保每个 batch 内无高 SCS pair，减少\n      Channel 2 type confusion，WrongType errors 从 2434 降至 680 (-72%)。Precision\n      轻微下降 (-12.8pp) 是因为小 batch 下模型倾向于 over-predict（与 exp-003a 中\n      low count 的 over-prediction pattern 一致），但 recall 的大幅提升远超 precision 损失。\n      Graph coloring 产生 k=10 batches 是因为 Few-NERD 的 66 types 中约 142 pair SCS>0.5，\n      形成中等密度的 confusability graph，chromatic number 为 10。10 个 batch 的\n      parallelized wall-clock 约 95s (vs single-pass 48s)，开销可接受。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 8: SDGD-zero vs Single-Pass on Few-NERD\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"Prec\", \"Recall\", \"WrongType\", \"API Calls\", \"Wall Clock (s)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass (66 types)\", 0.414, 0.648, 0.304, 2434, 1, 48]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero (k=10)\", 0.490, 0.520, 0.462, 680, 10, 385]\n          - [\"Δ\", \"+7.6pp\", \"-12.8pp\", \"+15.8pp\", \"-72%\", \"+9\", \"+337\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 7a: SDGD batch composition 可视化 — 10 个 batch 的 type 组成 heatmap，颜色编码 SCS。每个 batch 内 cell 均为冷色 (低 SCS)。\"\n      - \"Fig 7b: F1/Recall/Precision bar chart — single-pass vs SDGD-zero。SDGD 的 recall bar 显著高于 single-pass。\"\n      - \"Fig 7c: WrongType error reduction waterfall — 2434 → 680，按 batch 展示 type confusion 的减少。\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-zero 在 Few-NERD 上实现 +7.6 F1 点增益，核心驱动力是 recall 提升 (+15.8pp)\n      和 WrongType reduction (-72%)。Graph coloring 产生的 k=10 batches 在 batch size\n      和 confusability 之间取得平衡——每个 batch 平均 6.6 types 足够小以避免 capacity\n      bottleneck，且 batch 内无 SCS>0.5 的 confusable pair。这是第一个 principled\n      schema decomposition 结果，直接 operationalize 了 Claim 1-2 的发现。\n\n  - name: \"SDGD-zero on MAVEN\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      SDGD-zero on MAVEN (168 event types)。Cross-task validation of SDGD framework。\n      与 single-pass + random batching 对比。\n    expected_results:\n      scs_threshold_tau: 0.35\n      n_edges_in_graph: 1380\n      chromatic_number: 18\n      avg_types_per_batch: 9.3\n      max_types_per_batch: 14\n      min_types_per_batch: 5\n      # --- Performance ---\n      single_pass_f1: 0.08\n      single_pass_recall: 0.05\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.14\n      sdgd_zero_precision: 0.16\n      sdgd_zero_recall: 0.125\n      f1_gain_over_single_pass: 6.0\n      # --- Random batching (same k=18) ---\n      random_k18_f1: 0.11\n      random_k18_recall: 0.095\n      sdgd_vs_random_delta: 3.0\n      # --- Latency ---\n      sdgd_zero_api_calls: 18\n      sdgd_zero_wall_clock_s: 720\n      # --- WrongType ---\n      single_pass_wrong_type: 11500\n      sdgd_zero_wrong_type: 3200\n      wrong_type_reduction_pct: 72\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 的 168 types 和 FrameNet 层级结构使 confusability 效应更极端。\n      Single-pass F1 仅 0.08 (recall 0.05)，因为 168 types 的 prompt 远超模型的\n      effective schema capacity。SDGD-zero 用 τ=0.35 (比 Few-NERD 的 0.5 低，\n      因为 MAVEN 的 SCS 分布整体偏低 mean=0.216) 构建 confusability graph，\n      graph coloring 得 k=18 batches (avg 9.3 types)。F1 提升 +6.0 points 的来源：\n      (1) batch size 从 168 降到 avg 9.3，recall 从 0.05 提升到 0.125；(2) batch 内\n      无 FrameNet sibling pair，WrongType 从 11500 降到 3200 (-72%)。Random batching\n      (same k=18) 只得到 F1=0.11 (+3pp vs single-pass)，因为随机分组仅获得\n      count reduction 收益但不消除 confusability (random 的 batch 内仍有\n      ~7% 的高 SCS pairs)。SDGD vs random Δ=3.0 points 精确量化了\n      confusability-aware grouping 在 count reduction 之上的额外贡献。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 9: SDGD-zero vs Baselines on MAVEN (168 types)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"Prec\", \"Recall\", \"WrongType\", \"API Calls\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass (168)\", 0.08, 0.15, 0.05, 11500, 1]\n          - [\"Random (k=18)\", 0.11, 0.14, 0.095, 5800, 18]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero (k=18)\", 0.14, 0.16, 0.125, 3200, 18]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 8: MAVEN comparison bar chart — single-pass vs random vs SDGD-zero。三组 F1/Recall/WrongType bars。SDGD 在所有指标上优于 random，random 优于 single-pass。\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-zero 在 MAVEN 上的 +6.0 F1 增益 (和 vs random 的 +3.0 Δ) 证明 confusability-\n      aware decomposition 跨任务有效。MAVEN 的更大 type 空间 (168 vs 66) 使 count\n      reduction 本身就带来显著收益 (random +3pp)，但 SDGD 在此基础上再加 3pp，\n      量化了 confusability channel 的独立贡献。\n\n  - name: \"SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      用 5-10 个 calibration examples 构建 empirical confusion matrix，替代 embedding SCS\n      进行 graph coloring。与 SDGD-zero 对比。\n    expected_results:\n      calibration_examples: 8\n      calibration_api_calls: 8\n      calibration_wall_clock_s: 380\n      empirical_confusion_pairs_detected: 86\n      # --- Performance ---\n      sdgd_cal_f1: 0.505\n      sdgd_cal_precision: 0.530\n      sdgd_cal_recall: 0.483\n      sdgd_cal_k: 9\n      f1_gain_over_sdgd_zero: 1.5\n      f1_gain_over_single_pass: 9.1\n      # --- Comparison ---\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.490\n      sdgd_cal_vs_zero_delta: 1.5\n      # --- SCS vs empirical agreement ---\n      scs_empirical_overlap_top50: 0.72\n    result_rationale: >\n      SDGD-cal 通过 8 个 calibration 样本捕获 model-specific 的 confusion pattern，\n      而非依赖通用 embedding 距离。Empirical confusion matrix 发现了 86 个实际 confusion\n      pairs，其中 72% 也被 SCS 预测到，但有 28% 是 SCS 遗漏的 (如模型对特定 entity\n      naming pattern 的 confusion，不完全由 type label embedding 距离预测)。这些\n      额外信息使 graph coloring 更精确，产生 k=9 batches (vs SDGD-zero 的 k=10)，\n      实际更少 batch 但 confusability 分离更彻底。F1 提升 +1.5pp over SDGD-zero，\n      主要来自 recall (+2.1pp) 和 WrongType 进一步减少。增益幅度有限 (1.5pp) 是因为\n      embedding SCS 已经是 decent proxy (72% overlap)，calibration 只修正了 edge cases。\n      额外的 8 API calls 用于 calibration，total overhead 可接受。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 10: SDGD Variants Comparison (Few-NERD)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"Prec\", \"Recall\", \"k\", \"Total API Calls\", \"Setup Cost\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass\", 0.414, 0.648, 0.304, 1, 1, \"—\"]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero\", 0.490, 0.520, 0.462, 10, 10, \"0 (embedding only)\"]\n          - [\"SDGD-cal\", 0.505, 0.530, 0.483, 9, \"9+8cal=17\", \"8 calibration runs\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 9: SDGD-zero vs SDGD-cal 的 batch composition 对比 — 两组 heatmap 显示 calibration 如何调整 batch 分配 (标注移动的 types)。\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-cal 比 SDGD-zero 提升 1.5 F1 点，验证了 empirical confusability 优于\n      embedding proxy。但提升幅度有限，说明 SCS embedding 已经是 reasonably good proxy，\n      这反过来支持了 SCS 作为 practical zero-shot confusability measure 的可用性。\n      SDGD-cal 的 9.1pp gain over single-pass 接近 best-tier 上限 (10pp)。\n\n  - name: \"SDGD-cal on MAVEN\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: >\n      SDGD-cal on MAVEN (168 types) with calibration。Full comparison table。\n    expected_results:\n      calibration_examples: 10\n      calibration_api_calls: 10\n      sdgd_cal_f1: 0.16\n      sdgd_cal_precision: 0.175\n      sdgd_cal_recall: 0.148\n      sdgd_cal_k: 16\n      f1_gain_over_single_pass: 8.0\n      f1_gain_over_sdgd_zero: 2.0\n      sdgd_cal_vs_random_delta: 5.0\n      sdgd_cal_wrong_type: 2400\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 的 FrameNet 层级使 calibration 的价值更高：embedding SCS 对 hierarchically\n      related 但 functionally distinct 的 event types (如 Becoming_a_member vs Participation)\n      可能过估 confusability，而 calibration 发现这些 pair 实际不常混淆。反之，某些\n      linguistically similar triggers (如 \"killed\" → Killing vs Death) 的 confusion 被\n      SCS 低估但 calibration 捕获。结果 SDGD-cal 比 SDGD-zero 多 2.0pp (vs Few-NERD\n      的 1.5pp)，因为更大 type 空间下 SCS proxy error 的累积效应更明显。k=16 < SDGD-zero\n      的 k=18，fewer batches 但 confusability 分离更优，总 API 开销更低。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 11: Full MAVEN Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"Prec\", \"Recall\", \"WrongType\", \"k\", \"API Calls\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass\", 0.08, 0.15, 0.05, 11500, 1, 1]\n          - [\"Random (k=18)\", 0.11, 0.14, 0.095, 5800, 18, 18]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero\", 0.14, 0.16, 0.125, 3200, 18, 18]\n          - [\"SDGD-cal\", 0.16, 0.175, 0.148, 2400, 16, \"16+10cal=26\"]\n          - [\"Per-type\", 0.145, 0.13, 0.165, 450, 168, 168]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 10: Full comparison radar chart — 5 methods × 4 metrics (F1, Recall, 1-WrongType_rate, 1/API_calls)。SDGD-cal 在 quality-efficiency frontier 上 dominant。\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN full comparison 展示 SDGD-cal 在 quality-efficiency Pareto frontier 上的\n      优势：F1=0.16 略高于 per-type 的 0.145 (ratio=1.10)，API 开销仅 26 vs 168 calls。\n      Per-type recall 更高 (0.165 vs 0.148) 但 precision 更低 (0.13 vs 0.175)，因为\n      per-type 的单类型 batch 导致严重 over-prediction (没有 cross-type context\n      约束)。SDGD-cal 保留了 batch 内 non-confusable types 的 cross-type context，\n      对 precision 有正面效果。\n\n  - name: \"Random Batching Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: >\n      Few-NERD 上 random batching (same k=10 as SDGD)。\n      隔离 confusability-aware grouping vs batch count reduction 的各自贡献。\n    expected_results:\n      random_k10_f1: 0.455\n      random_k10_precision: 0.490\n      random_k10_recall: 0.425\n      random_k10_wrong_type: 1580\n      random_k10_avg_batch_bcs: 0.42\n      sdgd_zero_avg_batch_bcs: 0.18\n      # --- Decomposition ---\n      gain_from_count_reduction: 4.1\n      gain_from_confusability_reduction: 3.5\n      total_sdgd_gain: 7.6\n      additivity_ratio: 1.0\n      # --- Variance across random seeds ---\n      random_f1_std_across_5_seeds: 0.012\n      random_f1_range: [0.441, 0.468]\n      sdgd_consistently_better: true\n      # --- Significance ---\n      paired_t_sdgd_vs_random: 4.82\n      paired_t_p: 0.0004\n    result_rationale: >\n      Random batching with k=10 将 66 types 随机分成 10 组 (avg 6.6 per batch)，\n      获得与 SDGD 相同的 count reduction 但不优化 confusability。F1=0.455 vs\n      single-pass 0.414 = +4.1pp，纯 count reduction 贡献。SDGD F1=0.490 vs\n      random 0.455 = +3.5pp，纯 confusability reduction 贡献。两者近乎 additive\n      (4.1 + 3.5 = 7.6 = total gain)，与 exp-006 的 2×2 additive interaction 一致。\n      Random 的 avg batch BCS=0.42 (未优化，随机分配时 confusable pairs 仍有 ~35%\n      概率同批)，SDGD 的 avg batch BCS=0.18 (graph coloring 确保无 SCS>0.5 pair)。\n      WrongType: random 1580 vs SDGD 680——random 比 single-pass (2434) 减少 35%\n      (仅因 batch size 减小导致部分 confusable pairs 被分开)，SDGD 减少 72%\n      (系统性消除)。5 random seeds 的 F1 std=0.012 表明 random 结果相对稳定，\n      SDGD 在所有 seed 下 consistently better (paired t-test p=0.0004)。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 12: Gain Decomposition (Few-NERD)\"\n        columns: [\"Source\", \"ΔF1\", \"ΔRecall\", \"ΔWrongType\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Count reduction (random−SP)\", \"+4.1pp\", \"+12.1pp\", \"−35%\"]\n          - [\"Confusability reduction (SDGD−random)\", \"+3.5pp\", \"+3.7pp\", \"−57%\"]\n          - [\"Total (SDGD−SP)\", \"+7.6pp\", \"+15.8pp\", \"−72%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 11: Waterfall chart — F1 从 single-pass (0.414) 到 random (0.455) 到 SDGD (0.490)，两段分别标注 count reduction 和 confusability reduction 贡献。\"\n      - \"Fig 11b: 5 random seeds 的 F1 boxplot vs SDGD 的单点 (horizontal line)。SDGD consistently above all random runs。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Ablation 干净地分离了 SDGD 增益的两个来源：count reduction (+4.1pp, 54%) 和\n      confusability reduction (+3.5pp, 46%)。两者近乎完美 additive，进一步验证了\n      multi-channel model。这个结果直接回应潜在 reviewer concern \"为什么不直接\n      random split?\"——因为 random split 丢失了 confusability channel 的全部贡献，\n      在 Few-NERD 上损失 3.5 F1 点。SDGD vs random Δ=3.5pp 在 best-tier [2, 6] 内。\n\n  - name: \"Per-Type Splitting Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: >\n      Per-type splitting (UniNER-style, k=66 batches, 1 type per batch) on Few-NERD。\n      Decomposition 收益上界和 latency-quality tradeoff。\n    expected_results:\n      per_type_k: 66\n      per_type_f1: 0.49\n      per_type_precision: 0.44\n      per_type_recall: 0.55\n      per_type_wrong_type: 0\n      per_type_api_calls: 66\n      per_type_wall_clock_s: 1650\n      per_type_wall_clock_parallel_s: 420\n      # --- Ratios ---\n      sdgd_vs_pertype_f1_ratio: 1.00\n      sdgd_vs_pertype_latency_ratio: 0.23\n      sdgd_vs_pertype_api_ratio: 0.15\n      # --- Per-type drawbacks ---\n      per_type_over_prediction_rate: 2.85\n      per_type_cross_type_false_positives: 890\n      per_type_dedup_conflicts: 312\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-type splitting 完全消除 confusability (每 batch 仅 1 type，WrongType=0)，\n      是 Channel 2 的理论上界。但它有两个代价：(1) 极高 latency (66 API calls，\n      即使 parallelized 也需 420s vs SDGD 的 95s)；(2) 失去 cross-type context——\n      当模型只被告知寻找一种类型时，它倾向于 over-predict (pred/gold ratio 2.85)，\n      将相关但不匹配的 entity 标为目标类型。这导致 precision=0.44 低于 SDGD 的 0.52。\n      F1=0.49 与 SDGD-zero 的 0.490 几乎相同 (ratio=1.00)，因为 per-type 的 recall\n      优势 (0.55 vs 0.462) 被 precision 劣势 (0.44 vs 0.52) 恰好抵消。\n      SDGD 实现了与 per-type 同等的 F1 但仅用 23% 的 wall-clock 时间和 15% 的\n      API calls，这是 SDGD 的核心 value proposition：通过 principled batch\n      composition 在 confusability reduction 和 cross-type context preservation\n      之间取得最优 tradeoff。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 13: SDGD vs Per-Type Splitting (Few-NERD)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"Prec\", \"Recall\", \"WrongType\", \"API Calls\", \"Wall Clock (s)\", \"Parallel (s)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass\", 0.414, 0.648, 0.304, 2434, 1, 48, 48]\n          - [\"Random (k=10)\", 0.455, 0.490, 0.425, 1580, 10, 350, 90]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero (k=10)\", 0.490, 0.520, 0.462, 680, 10, 385, 95]\n          - [\"SDGD-cal (k=9)\", 0.505, 0.530, 0.483, 520, 17, 560, 130]\n          - [\"Per-type (k=66)\", 0.490, 0.440, 0.550, 0, 66, 1650, 420]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 12: Quality-Latency Pareto frontier — x-axis: parallel wall-clock (log scale), y-axis: F1。Five methods 标注。SDGD-zero 和 SDGD-cal 在 frontier 上，per-type 在 frontier 外 (high latency, same/lower F1)。\"\n      - \"Fig 12b: Precision-Recall tradeoff scatter — per-type (high recall, low precision), SDGD (balanced), single-pass (high precision, low recall)。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-type splitting 验证了 confusability elimination 的理论上界 (WrongType=0)，\n      但 SDGD 以 1/4 的计算开销达到同等 F1。关键 insight：per-type splitting\n      over-corrects——消除 confusability 的同时也消除了 beneficial cross-type context\n      (模型知道其他类型存在时会更 conservative/precise about each type)。SDGD 保留\n      non-confusable types 在同一 batch 内的 mutual constraint effect，实现更好的\n      precision-recall balance。F1 ratio=1.00, latency ratio=0.23，均在 best-tier 范围内。\n\n  - name: \"SCS Embedding Proxy Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-015\"\n    description: >\n      Embedding SCS 与 empirical confusion matrix 的 rank correlation。\n      验证 embedding proxy 的实际有效性。\n    expected_results:\n      # --- Few-NERD ---\n      fewnerd_spearman_rho: 0.52\n      fewnerd_spearman_p: 1.8e-15\n      fewnerd_kendall_tau: 0.41\n      fewnerd_kendall_p: 3.2e-12\n      fewnerd_n_pairs: 1953\n      fewnerd_top20_overlap: 0.75\n      # --- MAVEN ---\n      maven_spearman_rho: 0.48\n      maven_spearman_p: 2.4e-18\n      maven_kendall_tau: 0.37\n      maven_kendall_p: 8.1e-15\n      maven_n_pairs: 14028\n      maven_top20_overlap: 0.70\n      # --- Threshold analysis ---\n      optimal_scs_threshold_fewnerd: 0.48\n      optimal_scs_threshold_maven: 0.33\n      threshold_f1_sensitivity: \"±0.1 around optimal → <1pp F1 change\"\n      # --- Failure cases ---\n      false_negative_pairs: 14\n      false_negative_example: \"product-food ↔ product-drink (SCS=0.38, empirical confusion=45)\"\n      false_positive_pairs: 22\n      false_positive_example: \"event-protest ↔ event-election (SCS=0.71, empirical confusion=2)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Embedding SCS 基于 type label 的语义 embedding 距离，与 empirical confusion 的\n      相关性取决于：(1) type confusion 是否主要由 label 语义相似性驱动 (是的，exp-002\n      已证明)，(2) embedding 空间是否准确反映 LLM 的内部 type representation (大体是，\n      因为都基于 transformer language model)。Spearman ρ=0.52 (Few-NERD) / 0.48 (MAVEN)\n      表示中等到强的 rank agreement。非 perfect (ρ<1) 的原因：(a) 某些 confusion 由\n      context 和 surface form 驱动而非 label semantics (如 person-other 和 person-artist\n      的 confusion 因为实际文本中 artist 常出现在 generic person context)；\n      (b) embedding distance 是对称的但 confusion 可能不对称 (A→B confusion ≠ B→A)。\n      Top-20 overlap 75% 说明 embedding proxy 捕获了大部分 critical confusion pairs。\n      14 个 false negative pairs (SCS 低但实际常混淆) 正好是 SDGD-cal 能额外捕获的，\n      解释了 SDGD-cal 比 SDGD-zero 提升 1.5pp 的来源。Threshold sensitivity ±0.1\n      导致 <1pp F1 change 说明 SDGD 对 τ 选择 robust。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table S2 (Supplementary): SCS Proxy Validation\"\n        columns: [\"Dataset\", \"Spearman ρ\", \"p\", \"Kendall τ\", \"p\", \"Top-20 Overlap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Few-NERD\", 0.52, \"1.8e-15\", 0.41, \"3.2e-12\", \"75%\"]\n          - [\"MAVEN\", 0.48, \"2.4e-18\", 0.37, \"8.1e-15\", \"70%\"]\n      - title: \"Table S3: SCS Threshold Sensitivity\"\n        columns: [\"τ\", \"SDGD k (FN)\", \"F1 (FN)\", \"SDGD k (MV)\", \"F1 (MV)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [0.3, 14, 0.484, 22, 0.135]\n          - [0.4, 12, 0.488, 20, 0.138]\n          - [0.5, 10, 0.490, 18, 0.140]\n          - [0.6, 8, 0.485, 15, 0.136]\n          - [0.7, 6, 0.470, 12, 0.125]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S2: SCS vs empirical confusion scatter — 每个点是一个 type pair，x=SCS, y=empirical confusion count。标注 false positive 和 false negative regions。\"\n      - \"Fig S3: Threshold sensitivity curve — x=τ, y=F1。平坦区间 [0.3, 0.6] 表明 SDGD robust to threshold choice。\"\n    analysis: >\n      SCS embedding proxy 在 ρ=0.48-0.52 水平有效，对 SDGD-zero 的实际性能足够。\n      Threshold sensitivity 分析显示 τ 在 [0.3, 0.6] 区间内 F1 变化 <1pp，使\n      SDGD-zero 成为 truly zero-shot method (无需 calibration 即可 deploy)。\n      False negative analysis 为 SDGD-cal 的额外价值提供了解释：calibration 发现\n      了 14 个 SCS 遗漏的 confusion pairs，将它们分到不同 batch 后 F1 额外提升 1.5pp。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3d59d397-8bee-498e-9e04-81525269ad2b","total_cost_usd":0.9409204999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14512,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":33388,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14512,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":33388,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14512,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14512},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":9465,"outputTokens":25,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.00959,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":33388,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":14512,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9313305,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"2fc5aad4-a236-420a-afbf-b52c5070c04b"}
